ck_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- v4.8.dev3\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev3 - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4080 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9186) - AMD Ryzen 7 7800X3D 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 63.11 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\n> [!note]\n> I only really noticed this issue when in a dev build but I think this could negatively affect lower end devices.\n\n`EditorHelpSearch::Runner::work` repeats `_fill` or `_slice` until a time threshold is exceeded this threshold is currently at 100ms meaning this only ensures that heavy searches result in a framerate <10 fps. I think a limit of 16ms (60fps) would be better so the UI can stay responsive when the search takes long.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n> As mentioned above I only really noticed this in a dev build so if you are in a normal build this may not be noticeable depending on you device\n\nIn `Script` open `Search Help`. Add and remove a character to the search to see if you can notice some lag.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs",